# Platform capabilities

Before inventing tagging, search, comments, flags, outbound events, mail, or
similar shared substrate in a custom addon, **prefer the matching
`framework/addons/` platform addon**. Authority for full contracts and HTTP
catalogs stays in `docs/sphinx/source/addon-*.md` and
`docs/sphinx/source/addons.md` (Platform addons). Exact import paths:
`framework-public-imports`.

## Practical author stack

Readiness-critical: `system` + `auth`. Typical hard stack:

`system` → `encryption` → `settings` → `auth` (+ `jobs` when enqueueing).

## Need → platform addon

| Need | Addon | Manifest edge | Do **not** invent |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Bases / pages / widgets / nav / seeds | `system` | hard `depends` (almost always) | Host edits under `applications/` or `framework/runtimes/` |
| Sessions / OAuth / rights / record rules | `auth` | hard when gated CRUD/UI | Parallel login or capability stacks |
| Settings store / categories / operator UI | `settings` | hard when defining or reading settings | Ad hoc config tables for operator settings |
| Secrets at rest (Fernet) | `encryption` | via settings/auth, or hard when calling helpers | Homegrown crypto for setting secrets |
| Background / scheduled work | `jobs` | hard when enqueueing | Direct Celery tasks outside job components |
| Shared Redis catalogs / pure snapshots | `cache` | prefer `optional_depends` + guarded bridge | Full `/api/pages` Redis cache — see `framework-cache-contracts` |
| File upload / shared attachment model | `attachments` | hard when storing files | Parallel blob tables without attachments |
| Public attachment URL routing | `cdn` | via attachments | Custom public URL schemes that bypass CDN contract |
| Outbound SMTP | `mail` | prefer `optional_depends` + optional bridge | One-off SMTP clients per addon |
| Outbound HTTP with retries | `http` | hard for integrations | Unbounded raw `requests` without retry policy |
| Inbound API rate limits | `ratelimit` | hard when shipping abuse controls | Ad hoc per-route counters |
| Change history / trust-boundary audit | `audit` | `optional_depends` when recording; hard for UI readers | Silent mutation logs outside audit |
| Principal inbox / delivery adapters | `notifications` | hard when producing notifications | Parallel inbox tables |
| Typed tags / polymorphic assignments | `tags` | hard when assigning or coercing tags | Home-grown tag tables/APIs |
| Threaded notes on `(model, id)` | `comments` | hard when embedding; else optional | Parallel comment schemas |
| ACL-filtered model-record search | `search` | hard when indexing/querying; else optional | Parallel full-text indexes per addon |
| CSV/JSON dump/restore for models | `impexp` | hard when offering portable dump/restore | One-off export scripts that skip registration |
| Outbound signed domain-event webhooks | `webhooks` | hard when calling `publish_event` | Unsigned ad hoc callback POSTs |
| Kill switches / principal / % rollout | `feature_flags` | hard when gating; else optional + guarded | Settings keys used as hot-path feature gates |
| ToS/Privacy clauses / consent banner / DSR | `legal` | hard when contributing categories/sections/banner | Product clauses stuffed into `framework/addons/legal` |
| Home destination setting | `homepage` | optional from auth; hard when reading helpers | Parallel “default landing” settings |
| User reports against model records | `report` | hard when offering report actions | Parallel report queues |
| Shared UI sounds | `sounds` | `optional_depends` when playing | Bundled one-off audio APIs |
| Demo sandbox widgets | `sandbox` | never required; omit in prod | Shipping sandbox as a hard dep |

## Decision rules

1. **Same generic capability across addons** → Substrate Check
   (`framework-addon-substrate` / hygiene). Extend platform; do not copy.
2. **Enhances but not required to boot** → `optional_depends` + deferred
   guarded bridge (never top-level import). Soft-fail when absent.
3. **Cannot register/run without it** → hard `depends` + normal imports.
   Direct imports need a **direct** depends entry; transitive is not enough.
4. **Product-tied logic** stays in the owning custom addon. Platform addons
   stay framework-agnostic (empty-`addons/` stranger still wants them).
5. Open the owning `docs/sphinx/source/addon-<name>.md` for HTTP catalogs and
   exact public import rows — do not fork those tables into this rule.

